# note: 2026-09-24: this file used to list 16 fields (provider, measurement_head, three digests, health_result, signature); the encoder writes the keyring, boot, verification, measurement, snapshot, health, rollback, freshness and provenance groups as well and has no signature in the digest stream. Corrected toward the encoder; no byte moved (RFC-0.33-003 D3).
# note: 2026-10-29: RFC-0.40-001 (closes E-094) bumped AttestationRecordV2::SCHEMA_VERSION 2 -> 3. Six availability bytes are written beside the claims they qualify (`boot.kernel_digest_available`, `verification.{release,rootfs,policy}_digest_available`, `measurement.available`, `snapshot.snapshot_digest_available`), and a claim whose flag is 0 is written as zero -- fixed width, zeroed by the encoder, the pattern `bundle-v1.frozen` states -- and a `verified_flags` bit is written only when its digest is available. The record used to assert, under a signature, that a release, a rootfs and a policy bundle had each been verified, over five literal digests and a literal chain head; the factory now says only what is true. The 2 -> 3 digest move is proved, not assumed: `tests/golden.rs::attestation_v3_is_v2_plus_six_flags` removes the six bytes, rewinds the version word and recovers the v2 golden.
# note: 2026-10-31: RFC-0.41-003 R2 moved the zeroing of `rollback.trust_provider_counter_value` into the encoder: it is written as 0 whenever `rollback.trust_provider_counter_supported` is 0, as every *_digest and the measurement section already were, rather than trusting the caller's raw value. `RollbackClaims` is `pub` with `pub` fields, so `AttestationRecordV2::local` mapping a failed read to 0 was the only honest path, not the only path. `SCHEMA_VERSION` stays 3 and no byte moved: every record the tree can construct sets the flag 1 beside its value, or 0 beside the 0 `local()` writes; the golden digest is unchanged, which is the instrument. The one new line in this file is the `note` that says so. Corrected toward the encoder (the precedent is the 2026-09-24 note above, RFC-0.33-003 D3).
# note: 2026-10-31: RFC-0.41-003 R1 (closes E-101) bumped AttestationRecordV2::SCHEMA_VERSION 3 -> 4, superseding the "stays 3" of the note above, which was true of that change (the counter value) and is not of this one. Five availability bytes are written, each immediately before the claim it qualifies -- `keyring.epochs_available` (the three `keyring.active_epoch_*`), `snapshot.id_available` (`snapshot.snapshot_id` and `snapshot.reason`), `health.status_available`, `rollback.last_advance_source_available`, `freshness.key_epoch_available` -- and the claim is written as zero when its flag is 0, by the encoder (one `note` line says so). Fixed width, zeroed by the encoder: the pattern this file already states for the digests. `snapshot.reason` and `health.status` get a flag although the factory already wrote 0, because 0 is a valid reason and a valid status, which is exactly the case a flag exists for. The 3 -> 4 digest move is proved, not assumed: `tests/golden.rs::attestation_v4_is_v3_plus_five_flags` removes the five bytes, rewinds the version word to 3 and recovers the v3 golden `241d4c91...b9`; the older chain to the v2 golden is kept (`attestation_v3_is_v2_plus_six_flags`). The golden for the sample moved 241d4c91...b9 -> adefb58c...ab69 and no field line of this file changed order or width: five field lines and one note line were added.
